window.docContents[67].resolve({"/UD-II___-expressions/Binary-operators/#Core-C______--UD-II___-expressions--Binary-operators":{"contents":"The arithmetic operators require int on both operands. The left operand is evaluated before the right one. Division and remainder truncate toward zero, as in C++, and a zero divisor is error.In the code, the case Binary of Eval.expr evaluates both operands and calls Eval.binop.\n\nEquality compares two int or two bool. Order compares two int. The result is bool.\n\nConjunction and disjunction require bool and short circuit. The second operand is evaluated only when the first one does not decide the result.In the code, the cases And and Or of Eval.expr implement the two pairs of rules.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009UD II, expressions","header":"3.4. Binary operators","id":"/UD-II___-expressions/Binary-operators/#Core-C______--UD-II___-expressions--Binary-operators"}});